2
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.797
This is Jacob Barnes reporting live for
AMT news from the St. Louis White House

3
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.595
where mourners
are being allowed in

4
00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.489
to pay their respects
to the late President.

5
00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.667
<i>As we await further details</i>

6
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.604
<i>in the apparent suicide
of Jeffrey Michener.</i>

7
00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.176
AMT news has confirmed that
the American hostages in Asia

8
00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.345
have been rescued.

9
00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:50.241
<i>It is unclear whether the President
was aware of this good news</i>

10
00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.612
<i>at the time of his death.</i>

11
00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.845
<i>In the absence of any
final note or message.</i>

12
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.988
<i>we can only speculate.</i>

13
00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.196
It seems that the pressures
of his embattled agenda.

14
00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.589
coupled with this
network's revelations

15
00:01:00.761 --> 00:01:03.321
of his culpability in the
Doak Stadium disaster.

16
00:01:03.664 --> 00:01:06.361
may have proved too much
for the President to bear.

17
00:01:11.138 --> 00:01:13.578
Vice President Oliver just
transferred to the C-130 in Panama.

18
00:01:13.707 --> 00:01:16.019
<i>He should be on the ground in
St. Louis in four and a half hours.</i>

19
00:01:16.043 --> 00:01:17.511
Is Judge Watkins on board?

20
00:01:17.678 --> 00:01:19.622
She's administering the
oath of office as we speak.

21
00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.705
<i>Good. That's good.</i>

22
00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.096
Please gather all of
our background and intel

23
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.679
on Peng and our Asian players.

24
00:01:28.956 --> 00:01:30.500
President Oliver's gonna
need to get up to speed

25
00:01:30.524 --> 00:01:32.001
before he speaks to
the regional leaders.

26
00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.789
Yes. ma'am.

27
00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.390
I've served under
six presidents.

28
00:02:04.658 --> 00:02:08.186
Jeffrey Michener is the only
one I ever shook hands with.

29
00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:15.131
<i>The people of new China send
our deepest respect and condolences</i>

30
00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:18.794
<i>to our brothers and
sisters in America.</i>

31
00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.904
<i>It is with great sadness
that we have learned of</i>

32
00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.738
<i>the death of President
Jeffrey Michener.</i>

33
00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:28.012
<i>President Michener
was an important ally.</i>

34
00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.409
<i>He's still in the mansion.</i>

35
00:02:30.584 --> 00:02:31.794
There's no way we're
getting back in there.

36
00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.962
if that's what you are thinking.

37
00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.386
We're in Tomahawk range.

38
00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:37.350
Tom. we don't even
know if he's actually there.

39
00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.969
He might have released this
video to bait us into attacking him.

40
00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.393
Happy to call that bluff.

41
00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.824
Okay. you take Peng out.

42
00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.074
his number two continues
with whatever their agenda is.

43
00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.644
<i>and we've just started a hot war
without knowing what their plans are.</i>

44
00:02:47.668 --> 00:02:50.068
why those boats are so important
to him. what he's smuggling.

45
00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.868
She's right. Much as I'd like
to take Peng out right now.

46
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.385
we gotta find Wu Ming
first. get to the bottom of this.

47
00:02:55.409 --> 00:02:57.776
That son of a bitch has been
pummeling us for 10 rounds.

48
00:02:58.078 --> 00:03:00.438
And I'm not much in the mood
to wait for his knockout punch.

49
00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.558
What about all the innocent
people in and around the mansion

50
00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.777
when your Tomahawk hits.

51
00:03:04.885 --> 00:03:06.683
<i>We can't just assassinate
a foreign leader</i>

52
00:03:07.054 --> 00:03:09.114
without consulting with
the commander in chief.

53
00:03:14.094 --> 00:03:17.030
Find me when you
get close to Shanzai.

54
00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.396
He blames himself.

55
00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.230
For what?

56
00:03:25.472 --> 00:03:28.237
Pushing Michener too
hard. Before he was ready.

57
00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.266
Did he?

58
00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.535
Country needed a president.

59
00:03:35.649 --> 00:03:37.845
Maybe we should find a
plane. Get Tom to St. Louis.

60
00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:42.117
He could help Oliver get his
bearings. give him some credibility.

61
00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:46.288
You saw him. He's
not going anywhere

62
00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:48.487
until we finish this.

63
00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.017
<i>Obviously. Jeffrey
Michener's are big shoes to fill.</i>

64
00:04:16.223 --> 00:04:18.385
<i>But Howard Oliver is
beloved here in St. Louis.</i>

65
00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.186
<i>where. as mayor. he oversaw</i>

66
00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.386
<i>the most effective
quarantine in the country.</i>

67
00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.526
<i>saving over 100.000
people during the plague.</i>

68
00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.876
It wasn't the first time.

69
00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.779
He tried to kill himself
on the <i>Nathan James.</i>

70
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.950
He slit his wrists.

71
00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:48.680
When Captain Chandler found
him. he'd nearly bled to death.

72
00:04:54.261 --> 00:04:55.422
I had no idea.

73
00:04:56.463 --> 00:04:57.692
I was on the ship. I...

74
00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:58.957
They kept it quiet.

75
00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:04.769
Only the senior leadership knew.

76
00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:10.535
Jeffrey told me when he felt
that he could finally trust me.

77
00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:19.442
I'm telling you this because you
need to stop beating yourself up.

78
00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.254
If anything. I'm the one.

79
00:05:23.924 --> 00:05:25.825
I knew he was suffering.

80
00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:31.654
I knew and I left him alone.

81
00:05:36.236 --> 00:05:37.465
Were the two of you...

82
00:05:45.779 --> 00:05:46.940
I'm so sorry. Allison.

83
00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:04.093
This one's a bust. too.

84
00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:05.659
Damn it.

85
00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:07.027
<i>Hey. Doc.</i>

86
00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.627
Is this something you need?

87
00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:13.005
That's... That's. uh...

88
00:06:14.341 --> 00:06:17.311
I don't even know what that is.
Dr. Scott never let me touch that machine.

89
00:06:17.611 --> 00:06:19.170
But I'm getting warmer?

90
00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.804
Yeah. sure.

91
00:06:22.649 --> 00:06:23.981
Hello.

92
00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:28.978
Hey. Doc. Looks like we
got a stowaway here. mate.

93
00:06:32.993 --> 00:06:34.154
Okay.

94
00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:37.362
This is very. very good.
This is a really good start.

95
00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:40.658
Um.

96
00:06:41.201 --> 00:06:43.112
could you guys start setting
this up over here for me?

97
00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.468
- You got it.
- Thanks.

98
00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.473
You wanted to see me?

99
00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:52.312
Kyoko has something to say to
you. She asked me to translate.

100
00:06:59.653 --> 00:07:03.249
She says that you saved her life. But
more importantly. you saved her son.

101
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.655
That was all Logan and
Rios. I didn't really do much.

102
00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.827
She says she hasn't
prayed since she was a child.

103
00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:21.333
But now she will every day.
for the doctors and for you.

104
00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:29.238
No. please. You don't have to
get up. It's okay. Ma'am. it's...

105
00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:56.071
<i>She says you are a natural.</i>

106
00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:19.898
<i>President...</i>

107
00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:24.169
<i>Mr. President. please.</i>

108
00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:01.167
Seems like the weather
matches our mood.

109
00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:03.870
- Welcome home. Mr. President.
- Thank you.

110
00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:10.984
The world's lost a great leader.

111
00:09:11.151 --> 00:09:15.680
But we. in this room. we've
lost a colleague and a friend.

112
00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:17.522
<i>You all served him well.</i>

113
00:09:17.724 --> 00:09:20.455
<i>And I look forward to continuing
the work you began together</i>

114
00:09:20.727 --> 00:09:24.220
as we navigate our way
through this difficult time.

115
00:09:44.384 --> 00:09:46.683
I'll need all of your
help getting up to speed.

116
00:09:46.853 --> 00:09:50.551
But first. I'll need to
speak to Captain Chandler.

117
00:09:53.193 --> 00:09:54.873
<i>St. Louis connected. sir.</i>

118
00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:59.092
- This is Captain Chandler.
<i>- Stand by for the President.</i>

119
00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:04.030
<i>- Captain Chandler.</i>
- Mr. President.

120
00:10:04.838 --> 00:10:09.401
<i>I am so very sorry. I know
how close you and Jeffrey were.</i>

121
00:10:10.677 --> 00:10:15.342
I hope that over time. I can
earn the trust and confidence

122
00:10:15.582 --> 00:10:17.414
<i>that you and he shared.</i>

123
00:10:18.084 --> 00:10:19.108
Yes. sir.

124
00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:21.950
<i>I have a lot to catch you up on.</i>

125
00:10:22.555 --> 00:10:25.252
We're currently approaching
the pirate haven of Shanzai

126
00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:28.587
where we intend to find a smuggler
who goes by the name of Wu Ming.

127
00:10:29.362 --> 00:10:30.673
We think he might
be able to help

128
00:10:30.697 --> 00:10:33.360
fill in the blanks about
why our people were taken.

129
00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:35.728
about ships painted
with black circles.

130
00:10:35.935 --> 00:10:37.961
and what President
Peng is planning in Asia.

131
00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:40.399
<i>Sir. I intend to
complete the mission</i>

132
00:10:40.573 --> 00:10:42.565
<i>that was given to me
by President Michener.</i>

133
00:10:43.643 --> 00:10:45.635
with your permission.

134
00:10:46.079 --> 00:10:49.572
<i>You have my permission
and my gratitude.</i>

135
00:10:50.817 --> 00:10:52.080
Thank you. Mr. President.

136
00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:02.586
We're 27 nautical miles
southeast of Shanzai port. sir.

137
00:11:04.197 --> 00:11:06.962
Vulture Team is standing by for
Captain Chandler and ready for infil

138
00:11:07.133 --> 00:11:08.624
as soon as Nomad
has eyes on target.

139
00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:11.965
All right. listen up. we got a
high-value target-capture mission.

140
00:11:12.305 --> 00:11:14.865
After beach entry. we
silent-patrol to the target.

141
00:11:15.074 --> 00:11:16.440
penetrate the perimeter defense.

142
00:11:16.609 --> 00:11:18.373
and we capture that
son of a bitch Wu Ming.

143
00:11:18.545 --> 00:11:20.207
We'll have an
immediate helo exfil.

144
00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.975
Last time we were in
Shanzai. it got hot. fast.

145
00:11:23.283 --> 00:11:24.444
So watch your six.

146
00:11:26.452 --> 00:11:28.421
Nathan James. <i>this is Nomad.</i>

147
00:11:28.588 --> 00:11:31.319
<i>going feet dry. six
klicks from Shanzai.</i>

148
00:11:35.061 --> 00:11:37.758
- Sonar.
- Nothing on subsurface.

149
00:11:38.231 --> 00:11:43.101
Radar tracking surface contact
bearing 2-5-8 heading 0-1-4 at 18 knots.

150
00:11:43.303 --> 00:11:45.772
AIS classifies it as
a shrimp cutter. sir.

151
00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:47.767
We are not taking any chances.

152
00:11:48.241 --> 00:11:51.234
All stations continue to
track and monitor that vessel.

153
00:11:51.744 --> 00:11:53.337
CNO on the bridge.

154
00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:54.924
Did you get the go from POTUS?

155
00:11:54.948 --> 00:11:57.059
He understands the importance
of what we're doing here.

156
00:11:57.083 --> 00:11:58.643
but has requested
proof-of-life videos.

157
00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:01.019
It's a morale boost
for back home.

158
00:12:01.921 --> 00:12:03.514
Land team is waiting for you.

159
00:12:04.857 --> 00:12:07.986
Nathan James. <i>this is
Nomad. Flag on the play.</i>

160
00:12:09.629 --> 00:12:10.927
Shanzai is a bust.

161
00:12:11.831 --> 00:12:13.265
<i>The place is a fire pit.</i>

162
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.024
The whole town?

163
00:12:15.301 --> 00:12:16.360
<i>Wiped out.</i>

164
00:12:17.303 --> 00:12:18.703
Nothing but ashes.

165
00:12:20.039 --> 00:12:21.530
<i>Nomad returning to ship.</i>

166
00:12:24.377 --> 00:12:26.812
He carpet-bombed
everybody to get one guy?

167
00:12:29.515 --> 00:12:31.006
Peng levelled Shanzai.

168
00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:34.183
Charred the place
to tie up loose ends.

169
00:12:34.988 --> 00:12:36.388
We assume Wu Ming's dead.

170
00:12:36.956 --> 00:12:39.619
But we still need to figure out
how he tracked all those ships.

171
00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:42.227
Especially the ones he
wanted you to stay away from.

172
00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:45.560
<i>Any idea if he might have
had a backup outside Shanzai?</i>

173
00:12:51.137 --> 00:12:52.628
It's a Chinese proverb.

174
00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:56.175
Wu Ming taught
me this when I asked

175
00:12:56.743 --> 00:13:00.236
why he never pirated
the ships himself.

176
00:13:01.147 --> 00:13:02.342
It means.

177
00:13:03.916 --> 00:13:09.753
"When children travel far from
home mothers never stop worrying."

178
00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.390
So he was a mama's boy?

179
00:13:16.162 --> 00:13:18.063
He supported her.

180
00:13:18.231 --> 00:13:21.201
his sister. the grandmother.

181
00:13:21.401 --> 00:13:23.836
And you think he may
have stashed intel with them.

182
00:13:24.404 --> 00:13:27.067
That way they could
carry on the business.

183
00:13:28.708 --> 00:13:31.940
He could provide for
them. even in death.

184
00:13:32.111 --> 00:13:33.856
<i>It's the only good thing
I ever heard about him.</i>

185
00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.007
Took care of his family.

186
00:13:35.948 --> 00:13:39.043
And where exactly might
we find Mama Ming?

187
00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:50.969
<i>Nathan James</i> will
loiter over the horizon

188
00:13:51.097 --> 00:13:54.067
while a VBSS team commandeers a
vehicle near the Beng Mu Chun inlet

189
00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:56.896
and then heads inland to Chin
Ma to find Wu Ming's family.

190
00:13:59.505 --> 00:14:01.201
Just awaiting
your approval. sir.

191
00:14:02.709 --> 00:14:03.709
Yes.

192
00:14:06.346 --> 00:14:07.678
Commander Green.

193
00:14:08.014 --> 00:14:10.279
How are we doing on
those proof-of-life videos

194
00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.713
from the rescued hostages?

195
00:14:11.884 --> 00:14:14.080
The <i>Nathan James</i> crew
is working on them. sir.

196
00:14:14.253 --> 00:14:16.933
But we are having some difficulty
with the visual signal on our end.

197
00:14:17.123 --> 00:14:18.901
I can get the audio
recordings for you right away.

198
00:14:18.925 --> 00:14:21.451
Audio isn't good enough.
We need to see faces.

199
00:14:21.627 --> 00:14:23.858
The American people need
to see that we had a win.

200
00:14:24.097 --> 00:14:27.124
Sort out that
technical glitch ASAP.

201
00:14:27.734 --> 00:14:28.734
Yes. sir.

202
00:14:31.037 --> 00:14:33.199
<i>Okay. Miller. This is for
everybody back home</i>

203
00:14:33.373 --> 00:14:35.274
<i>so they know you're
still taking up space.</i>

204
00:14:35.575 --> 00:14:37.373
<i>All right. go
ahead. start talking.</i>

205
00:14:38.111 --> 00:14:41.775
Hey. Ma. Now. don't be scared. I
know my face is a little messed up.

206
00:14:41.948 --> 00:14:43.726
but the doc promised
that I'll go back to being

207
00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.275
just as pretty as I was before.

208
00:14:45.918 --> 00:14:48.251
So. Freak from
Spider-Man. basically.

209
00:14:48.421 --> 00:14:51.255
Okay. man. A little respect.
This is for my mother.

210
00:14:51.724 --> 00:14:55.161
<i>Hey. Ma. Now. don't be scared. I
know my face is a little messed up.</i>

211
00:14:55.595 --> 00:14:57.272
<i>- but the doc promised...</i>
- Can you see anything at all?

212
00:14:57.296 --> 00:14:58.656
<i>Just as pretty as I was before.</i>

213
00:14:58.931 --> 00:15:01.043
- Still nothing.
<i>- So. Freak from Spider-Man. basically.</i>

214
00:15:01.067 --> 00:15:03.387
<i>- Okay. man. A little respect.</i>
- There it is again.

215
00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:06.102
<i>I miss you. Mom. I love you.</i>

216
00:15:06.672 --> 00:15:09.118
<i>Isn't this the same problem
you were working on with Val?</i>

217
00:15:09.142 --> 00:15:12.010
Yes. But there's hundreds
of hours of data to analyze.

218
00:15:12.178 --> 00:15:14.477
So we haven't been able to
figure out what's causing it.

219
00:15:14.847 --> 00:15:15.974
<i>With her gone...</i>

220
00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:18.346
<i>Damn. System just crashed.</i>

221
00:15:18.584 --> 00:15:20.644
I need to run downstairs to
the communications room.

222
00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:25.850
<i>Hurry. Dennis. We
need to fix this. Please.</i>

223
00:15:26.826 --> 00:15:28.317
How are you holding
up over there?

224
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:31.924
Alisha.

225
00:15:35.468 --> 00:15:37.494
<i>I'm the one who found Michener.</i>

226
00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:42.541
Oh. my... Kara.

227
00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.010
I'm sorry.

228
00:15:46.179 --> 00:15:49.445
You are over there risking
your lives. I'm sitting at a desk.

229
00:15:50.216 --> 00:15:51.216
- I shouldn't...
<i>- No.</i>

230
00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:54.451
We need you there.
Now more than ever.

231
00:16:03.563 --> 00:16:05.191
Vulture Team has
reached Chin Ma.

232
00:16:05.531 --> 00:16:07.796
- ETA to target?
<i>- Less than five minutes. sir.</i>

233
00:16:33.726 --> 00:16:35.558
Clear. Go.

234
00:17:00.253 --> 00:17:01.253
That's MSS.

235
00:17:01.454 --> 00:17:03.787
I guess Peng wants to
talk to Mama Ming. too.

236
00:17:21.874 --> 00:17:23.035
Ah!

237
00:17:26.379 --> 00:17:30.316
Well. he's still alive.

238
00:17:39.258 --> 00:17:40.692
All teams. sitrep. over.

239
00:17:40.893 --> 00:17:43.658
- Cooper. set.
- Green. set.

240
00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.355
<i>Taylor. go for entry.</i>

241
00:17:51.737 --> 00:17:53.399
<i>Burk's got eyes on upper target.</i>

242
00:17:53.839 --> 00:17:57.071
I got the shot on
the lower. Burk. go.

243
00:18:19.298 --> 00:18:20.527
Taylor. set.

244
00:18:24.604 --> 00:18:29.372
<i>Primary entry team. set.
All teams. on my count.</i>

245
00:18:30.209 --> 00:18:33.077
<i>Three. two. one.</i>

246
00:18:33.379 --> 00:18:34.379
<i>Execute.</i>

247
00:21:02.094 --> 00:21:03.562
How are you feeling. Wu Ming?

248
00:21:04.029 --> 00:21:05.759
Grateful we saved your life?

249
00:21:15.908 --> 00:21:17.706
<i>He says you brought
them to his door.</i>

250
00:21:18.444 --> 00:21:20.208
It's you who got
everybody in Shanzai killed.

251
00:21:20.613 --> 00:21:23.708
I didn't start this.
You and Peng did.

252
00:21:26.685 --> 00:21:28.551
<i>Why was Lau Hu torturing you?</i>

253
00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:39.596
Lottery tickets.

254
00:21:40.633 --> 00:21:44.400
How the hell does lottery even work
now? There's barely any currency.

255
00:21:44.637 --> 00:21:48.699
I've seen it in Hong Kong. mate.
People put in whatever they have.

256
00:21:49.074 --> 00:21:50.770
A chicken. a bag of rice.

257
00:21:50.943 --> 00:21:52.809
<i>They get a ticket.
a number's drawn.</i>

258
00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:54.807
Whoever wins.
takes the entire pot.

259
00:21:55.047 --> 00:21:58.074
<i>After the proprietor skims
some off the top. of course.</i>

260
00:21:58.884 --> 00:22:01.115
<i>Tell me about black
circles on ships.</i>

261
00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:09.625
He's hiding something.

262
00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:15.768
What's so precious
about those marked ships?

263
00:22:16.902 --> 00:22:18.803
Why would Peng
go to all this trouble?

264
00:22:35.821 --> 00:22:39.690
Why are you still protecting Peng
after everything he's done to you?

265
00:22:40.326 --> 00:22:43.626
I know nothing.
Nothing. Nothing!

266
00:23:01.213 --> 00:23:02.704
That look like a
hull number to you?

267
00:23:03.983 --> 00:23:05.542
Yes. it does.

268
00:23:06.452 --> 00:23:09.945
These digits here.
these are coordinates

269
00:23:10.656 --> 00:23:13.490
for the Strait of Malacca. the
biggest shipping lane in the region.

270
00:23:14.293 --> 00:23:16.194
<i>It's the intel Wu
Ming sells to pirates.</i>

271
00:23:16.629 --> 00:23:20.122
If each one of these lottery tickets
represents a ship and its location...

272
00:23:33.712 --> 00:23:34.736
Jackpot.

273
00:23:36.882 --> 00:23:38.248
Sir.

274
00:23:56.635 --> 00:23:57.864
You all right?

275
00:23:58.037 --> 00:23:59.938
I could have done
without Rivera's eulogy.

276
00:24:00.105 --> 00:24:01.971
Seems like he's already
jockeying for favor.

277
00:24:03.442 --> 00:24:07.777
I noticed that our lone senator was
conspicuously absent from the funeral.

278
00:24:07.947 --> 00:24:12.544
I spoke to Beatty. There was an attack
on a ration card facility in Bellingham.

279
00:24:13.052 --> 00:24:15.817
<i>He's sitting on a powder keg
up there. He couldn't get away.</i>

280
00:24:16.155 --> 00:24:17.214
Maybe.

281
00:24:17.389 --> 00:24:20.484
Or maybe he's sending a signal that
he's not in support of our administration.

282
00:24:20.693 --> 00:24:22.594
Well. the Senator
wasn't particularly fond

283
00:24:22.761 --> 00:24:25.162
of how the last president
used him as a rubber stamp.

284
00:24:25.464 --> 00:24:27.262
- Meaning?
<i>- Sir. you've been away.</i>

285
00:24:27.433 --> 00:24:29.673
I don't think you realize
what a mess this country is in.

286
00:24:29.702 --> 00:24:32.433
Maybe they don't remember what
a mess we had five months ago

287
00:24:32.805 --> 00:24:35.001
<i>before Michener and the</i>
James <i>came home with the cure.</i>

288
00:24:35.274 --> 00:24:37.834
No. they remember. sir. And
they are grateful for the cure.

289
00:24:38.177 --> 00:24:41.375
But that doesn't give the government
a free pass for everything else.

290
00:24:42.114 --> 00:24:43.446
Especially since people think

291
00:24:43.615 --> 00:24:45.811
that most of the decisions
that have come out of here

292
00:24:46.018 --> 00:24:47.018
have been disastrous.

293
00:24:47.186 --> 00:24:49.348
Hell. you can't even prove
you rescued your own people.

294
00:24:49.855 --> 00:24:52.381
<i>The pirates broadcast their faces
from a jungle across the globe</i>

295
00:24:52.558 --> 00:24:55.027
and you can't manage a Skype
call from a $3 billion warship?

296
00:24:55.194 --> 00:24:57.163
We're working nonstop
on the issue. Mr. President.

297
00:24:57.329 --> 00:24:58.807
I'm confident we'll
have it solved shortly.

298
00:24:58.831 --> 00:25:00.732
<i>Let's not lose the
forest for the trees.</i>

299
00:25:01.400 --> 00:25:03.665
We're all pleased that
the hostages are safe.

300
00:25:03.836 --> 00:25:05.702
and we're sure
you'll sort that out.

301
00:25:06.171 --> 00:25:08.731
The more pressing issue
is our domestic policy.

302
00:25:09.008 --> 00:25:10.499
<i>I think we can all agree</i>

303
00:25:10.676 --> 00:25:14.204
that Michener jumped too
quickly to federalize everything.

304
00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:17.973
If you were to curb some of his
measures. I'm sure it will go a long way

305
00:25:18.150 --> 00:25:20.312
to smoothing things
over with Senator Beatty

306
00:25:20.552 --> 00:25:22.077
and the American people.

307
00:25:22.254 --> 00:25:26.851
The ration card program has
been the chief cause of unrest.

308
00:25:27.159 --> 00:25:29.025
<i>And limits to bank withdrawals.</i>

309
00:25:29.194 --> 00:25:30.992
<i>The people do not
want the government</i>

310
00:25:31.163 --> 00:25:33.098
interfering with how
they spend their money.

311
00:25:33.332 --> 00:25:34.595
<i>Come on. Alex. It's all of it.</i>

312
00:25:34.867 --> 00:25:36.733
The land claim issues
are just as contentious.

313
00:25:36.935 --> 00:25:38.164
What do you all want?

314
00:25:39.571 --> 00:25:41.506
<i>To go back to dog-eat-dog?</i>

315
00:25:41.874 --> 00:25:43.914
That's appealing when
you're at the top of the heap.

316
00:25:44.676 --> 00:25:46.577
But there are people
out there going hungry

317
00:25:46.745 --> 00:25:49.271
while we are producing more
than enough food to feed everyone.

318
00:25:49.515 --> 00:25:51.755
That's why President Michener
started those ration cards.

319
00:25:52.851 --> 00:25:54.931
So that all of our citizens
can have their fair share

320
00:25:55.020 --> 00:25:57.140
- of what they need to get...
<i>- Commander Green.</i>

321
00:26:01.026 --> 00:26:05.122
If we need your advice as it
pertains to our military. we'll ask for it.

322
00:26:10.803 --> 00:26:13.102
Sir. I know that
you were skittish

323
00:26:13.572 --> 00:26:16.371
<i>about instituting these
policies from the beginning.</i>

324
00:26:16.542 --> 00:26:20.138
It doesn't matter what I thought
then or if they're unpopular.

325
00:26:22.147 --> 00:26:23.479
Are they working or not?

326
00:26:29.521 --> 00:26:31.641
I think it's fair to say that
these policies are doing

327
00:26:31.790 --> 00:26:33.986
more harm than good. sir.

328
00:26:38.864 --> 00:26:40.093
What happened in there?

329
00:26:40.332 --> 00:26:43.666
Everything we worked for. everything
President Michener stood for.

330
00:26:43.836 --> 00:26:46.704
We're in a crisis. It's our job
to hold the country together.

331
00:26:47.439 --> 00:26:50.932
You sat with the President
and wrote those policies.

332
00:26:51.376 --> 00:26:52.435
You didn't fight for them.

333
00:26:52.644 --> 00:26:54.322
If President Michener
couldn't make them work.

334
00:26:54.346 --> 00:26:56.008
then Howard
Oliver certainly can't.

335
00:26:57.549 --> 00:27:00.542
So you are going to let Oliver
capitulate to the regional leaders.

336
00:27:02.888 --> 00:27:05.050
He just gave them
authority over local militias

337
00:27:05.224 --> 00:27:06.715
<i>without speaking
to Captain Chandler.</i>

338
00:27:06.892 --> 00:27:08.369
Chandler is the acting
head of our military.

339
00:27:08.393 --> 00:27:09.704
and he never would
have allowed it.

340
00:27:09.728 --> 00:27:12.288
Captain Chandler
is 12.000 miles away.

341
00:27:12.798 --> 00:27:14.976
The regional leaders need to
be able to call their own shots.

342
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:16.960
If they can't control their
own regions. who will?

343
00:27:17.169 --> 00:27:19.570
They are the ones stoking
the unrest. President Michener...

344
00:27:19.805 --> 00:27:21.535
President Michener isn't here!

345
00:27:22.241 --> 00:27:23.903
He took the easy way out.

346
00:27:24.176 --> 00:27:25.336
So if they sit in that office

347
00:27:25.410 --> 00:27:28.073
and they reverse every decision
that he made as president.

348
00:27:28.313 --> 00:27:30.009
there's nobody to blame but him.

349
00:27:35.687 --> 00:27:36.916
Sir.

350
00:27:37.756 --> 00:27:39.190
Uh. thank you for coming down.

351
00:27:40.159 --> 00:27:41.718
<i>I've made some progress. sir.</i>

352
00:27:41.894 --> 00:27:44.989
<i>but I still have more
questions than answers.</i>

353
00:27:46.165 --> 00:27:49.158
This is an image of our
cure from Dr. Scott's notes.

354
00:27:49.434 --> 00:27:52.233
I've isolated the compound in
Takehaya and Kyoko's blood.

355
00:27:52.437 --> 00:27:53.637
It's exactly the same as ours.

356
00:27:54.173 --> 00:27:56.506
Structurally uncompromised.
as far as I can tell.

357
00:27:57.109 --> 00:28:00.511
This is an image of the
red flu from Dr. Scott's files.

358
00:28:00.913 --> 00:28:02.211
And this...

359
00:28:02.881 --> 00:28:04.873
<i>This is the virus
in Kyoko's blood.</i>

360
00:28:06.018 --> 00:28:07.018
It's different.

361
00:28:07.753 --> 00:28:09.449
- Bulkier.
- Exactly.

362
00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:12.283
That bulkiness is present
in Takehaya's virus as well.

363
00:28:12.758 --> 00:28:16.217
The virus in their blood is
similar enough to the original

364
00:28:16.395 --> 00:28:18.261
that my preliminary
tests identified it.

365
00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:20.729
- But it is somewhat altered.
- A mutation.

366
00:28:21.233 --> 00:28:24.226
I can't say for sure. But
whatever is causing the bulkiness

367
00:28:24.436 --> 00:28:26.029
is preventing the
cure from working.

368
00:28:26.405 --> 00:28:29.050
That means everyone on this ship
who has come in contact with Takehaya

369
00:28:29.074 --> 00:28:30.874
- could be infected.
- That was my worry. too.

370
00:28:30.943 --> 00:28:33.071
But none of us from the prison
camp have any symptoms.

371
00:28:33.645 --> 00:28:36.444
I crossed the virus
in Takehaya's blood

372
00:28:36.648 --> 00:28:38.583
with a sample of my own
and from several sailors

373
00:28:38.784 --> 00:28:42.448
who had no contact with Takehaya.
Kyoko or any of us who were prisoners.

374
00:28:42.955 --> 00:28:45.220
The bulkier virus
doesn't make us sick.

375
00:28:45.824 --> 00:28:48.487
Somehow the cure in
us defends against it.

376
00:28:48.927 --> 00:28:52.420
If Takehaya and Kyoko
both have the same cure.

377
00:28:53.232 --> 00:28:54.666
why is the virus harming them?

378
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:57.765
I wish I knew. sir.
I'll keep digging.

379
00:28:58.770 --> 00:29:03.003
We're at 19.83
North by 112.5 East.

380
00:29:03.342 --> 00:29:05.607
Course 1-0-0.
speed 20 knots. sir.

381
00:29:05.844 --> 00:29:07.073
There's a small landmass here.

382
00:29:07.246 --> 00:29:09.772
which should provide cover
from hostile radar detection

383
00:29:09.948 --> 00:29:13.441
while giving us a vantage point on
the shipping lane indicated on that card.

384
00:29:13.652 --> 00:29:15.563
Helo is standing by
to execute flyovers.

385
00:29:15.587 --> 00:29:18.648
We expect many vessels to have
AIS switched off on account of pirates.

386
00:29:30.302 --> 00:29:36.173
She's Alpha-Charlie-Foxtrot
7-9-8-3-1-3-9-6.

387
00:29:36.808 --> 00:29:38.003
Any other markings?

388
00:29:38.277 --> 00:29:41.270
<i>Uh. just a couple of dings
from a bad parking job.</i>

389
00:29:41.613 --> 00:29:42.808
<i>No black dot.</i>

390
00:29:44.182 --> 00:29:45.206
No dice.

391
00:29:45.550 --> 00:29:47.883
Is it possible the ship
already passed this location?

392
00:29:48.186 --> 00:29:50.064
According to Wu Ming's
intel. it was last pinged

393
00:29:50.088 --> 00:29:52.421
outside Hainan Harbor
yesterday at 2200 hours.

394
00:29:52.891 --> 00:29:54.223
Even a wave-piercing catamaran

395
00:29:54.559 --> 00:29:56.519
couldn't traverse this
shipping lane that quickly.

396
00:29:56.695 --> 00:29:57.695
<i>Captain.</i>

397
00:29:57.896 --> 00:29:59.592
Radar's tracking
small surface vessel

398
00:29:59.831 --> 00:30:01.993
approaching our contact
point on the shipping lane.

399
00:30:02.267 --> 00:30:05.829
Nomad. vessel
approaching south at 0-2-5.

400
00:30:06.038 --> 00:30:07.438
Initiate flyover.

401
00:30:07.606 --> 00:30:10.041
<i>Roger that.</i> Nathan
James. <i>Making the turn.</i>

402
00:30:14.713 --> 00:30:16.511
I don't know about
this one. Captain.

403
00:30:16.682 --> 00:30:17.922
<i>What's wrong with it?</i>

404
00:30:18.016 --> 00:30:19.216
There's nothing wrong with it.

405
00:30:19.351 --> 00:30:21.286
<i>if you are on
spring break in Ibiza.</i>

406
00:30:21.687 --> 00:30:22.847
What the hell does that mean?

407
00:30:22.954 --> 00:30:26.015
<i>It's a 120-foot pleasure
cruiser. No cargo hold.</i>

408
00:30:26.358 --> 00:30:27.724
Wait a second.

409
00:30:28.060 --> 00:30:33.055
<i>Alpha-Zulu-Bravo-7-9-8-6-3-Lima-3-0-9.</i>

410
00:30:33.231 --> 00:30:34.290
That's it.

411
00:30:34.466 --> 00:30:37.231
And we're staring at a big
old dark side of the moon.

412
00:31:04.062 --> 00:31:08.397
Vessel Encore. 0-1-4. 22 knots.
This is US Navy warship 1-5-1

413
00:31:08.567 --> 00:31:10.058
<i>requesting to
board for inspection</i>

414
00:31:10.235 --> 00:31:12.275
<i>in accordance with the
International Law of the Sea.</i>

415
00:31:20.445 --> 00:31:22.937
Vessel Encore. 0-1-4. 22 knots.

416
00:31:23.582 --> 00:31:24.582
<i>I say again.</i>

417
00:31:24.750 --> 00:31:28.482
<i>This is US Navy warship 1-5-1
requesting to board for inspection</i>

418
00:31:29.020 --> 00:31:31.580
<i>in accordance with the
International Law of the Sea.</i>

419
00:31:31.957 --> 00:31:35.519
TAO. surface tracks 7-2-8-7-1
increasing speed to 25 knots.

420
00:31:35.861 --> 00:31:36.920
Captain. TAO.

421
00:31:37.095 --> 00:31:39.189
<i>Surface contact maybe
trying to make a run for it.</i>

422
00:31:39.364 --> 00:31:41.609
XO. let's stick our nose out.
let him know he has company.

423
00:31:41.633 --> 00:31:44.933
OOD. increase speed to 25
knots. Come to 1.000 yards CPA.

424
00:32:04.322 --> 00:32:07.656
TAO. surface tracks 7-2-8-7-1
coming to course 0-4-5.

425
00:32:07.859 --> 00:32:09.521
increasing speed to 35 knots.

426
00:32:09.694 --> 00:32:10.694
They're trying to evade.

427
00:32:10.896 --> 00:32:12.573
Just turn starboard
and increase speed. sir.

428
00:32:12.597 --> 00:32:16.090
Starboard ROC. fire MK-38. one
salvo warning shots across the bow.

429
00:32:16.368 --> 00:32:18.746
Prepare countermeasures. But
do not. under any circumstances.

430
00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:20.705
sink that ship. Not till
we know what's aboard.

431
00:32:20.872 --> 00:32:21.896
Aye. Captain.

432
00:32:22.073 --> 00:32:23.598
All stations. stand
by to re-engage.

433
00:32:36.288 --> 00:32:39.554
Sir. he's changed course to 2-5-0.
He's headed for the Yanshi Atoll.

434
00:32:39.724 --> 00:32:40.724
OOD. all ahead full.

435
00:32:40.892 --> 00:32:42.904
Sir. we can't outrun him.
He's traveling at 36 knots.

436
00:32:42.928 --> 00:32:45.625
And we can't go into the atoll.
the coral beds are too shallow.

437
00:32:46.097 --> 00:32:47.292
XO. time to close the net.

438
00:32:47.599 --> 00:32:49.568
Nomad. you are go for approach.

439
00:32:49.968 --> 00:32:52.870
All right. boys and girls.
Let's drop in for a cocktail.

440
00:33:12.591 --> 00:33:14.457
TAO. surface tracks
vessel. 1.000 yards.

441
00:33:14.659 --> 00:33:17.595
Captain. TAO. Surface
contact 10 degrees relative.

442
00:33:24.269 --> 00:33:27.933
<i>Okay. don't do it.
buddy. Not a good move.</i>

443
00:33:28.507 --> 00:33:30.237
<i>Don't do anything stupid.</i>

444
00:33:30.408 --> 00:33:31.842
<i>- Cut your engine.</i>
- Shit. man.

445
00:33:32.477 --> 00:33:35.675
<i>We are US Navy. Lay
down your weapon!</i>

446
00:33:36.414 --> 00:33:39.350
<i>We don't want to hurt you. but
we will be boarding your vessel.</i>

447
00:33:40.151 --> 00:33:42.620
<i>Nathan James.</i>
vessel is surrendering.

448
00:33:44.456 --> 00:33:45.822
Game over. asshole.

449
00:33:54.165 --> 00:33:56.031
<i>Is this even necessary. yo?</i>

450
00:33:56.268 --> 00:33:58.828
Tell us where Peng's cargo
is. and we'll stop right now.

451
00:33:59.871 --> 00:34:01.999
Does this even look
like a cargo ship to you?

452
00:34:02.874 --> 00:34:04.274
<i>We tossed the whole vessel.</i>

453
00:34:04.442 --> 00:34:07.037
All we found were
a couple more M16s

454
00:34:07.379 --> 00:34:08.779
and a case of Cristal.

455
00:34:08.947 --> 00:34:10.313
See? What did I tell you?

456
00:34:10.482 --> 00:34:13.782
If you got nothing to hide. then
why run from a US Navy ship?

457
00:34:14.019 --> 00:34:15.851
It's the apocalypse. man.

458
00:34:16.054 --> 00:34:18.546
All kinds of people get
into all kinds of boats

459
00:34:18.723 --> 00:34:19.986
saying all kinds of shit.

460
00:34:20.158 --> 00:34:21.878
You could have been
pirates. for all I know.

461
00:34:22.627 --> 00:34:25.222
This is my boat. You
can't take it from me.

462
00:34:25.964 --> 00:34:28.559
Oh. yeah? You got bills of
sales for those weapons?

463
00:34:30.035 --> 00:34:32.475
<i>Well. then you are in violation
of International Maritime Law.</i>

464
00:34:32.671 --> 00:34:35.004
The US Navy has the right
to place you under arrest

465
00:34:35.173 --> 00:34:36.801
and commandeer this vessel.

466
00:34:37.242 --> 00:34:41.009
Hell. no. This is my
baby. You can't do this. yo.

467
00:34:41.346 --> 00:34:42.405
We sure can. yo.

468
00:34:42.681 --> 00:34:45.981
You wanna keep your
precious ship. you start talking.

469
00:34:48.153 --> 00:34:49.314
Americans.

470
00:34:49.888 --> 00:34:51.720
So self-righteous.

471
00:35:09.107 --> 00:35:10.166
Move.

472
00:35:12.043 --> 00:35:14.205
Well. that's cocaine. heroin.

473
00:35:14.546 --> 00:35:17.243
- How much more of this have you got?
- Five more crates.

474
00:35:18.049 --> 00:35:20.518
Come on. yo. This can't
even be illegal anymore.

475
00:35:20.919 --> 00:35:23.787
The people have suffered
enough. I'm just meeting needs.

476
00:35:24.022 --> 00:35:25.388
Where'd you pick it up?

477
00:35:25.857 --> 00:35:27.223
An island up at Hainan.

478
00:35:28.093 --> 00:35:31.530
Chinese MSS dudes loaded me
up. I don't want to mess with them.

479
00:35:40.705 --> 00:35:42.264
Peng doesn't bother with drugs.

480
00:35:43.775 --> 00:35:45.607
Hey. what are you doing. yo?

481
00:35:45.777 --> 00:35:48.747
You know what my suppliers will do
to me if even one of those is missing?

482
00:35:49.114 --> 00:35:50.138
Shut up.

483
00:36:06.931 --> 00:36:08.229
Holy shit!

484
00:36:09.067 --> 00:36:11.798
<i>The missile's clearly been
retrofitted since its manufacture.</i>

485
00:36:12.303 --> 00:36:13.943
<i>Has to be a chemical
weapon of some kind.</i>

486
00:36:14.472 --> 00:36:17.499
He picked up those crates
100 miles southeast of Hainan.

487
00:36:17.676 --> 00:36:19.008
Paraiso Island.

488
00:36:19.177 --> 00:36:21.257
You sure that trafficker
didn't know what was in 'em?

489
00:36:21.346 --> 00:36:23.941
He was perfectly happy being
a run-of-the-mill drug runner.

490
00:36:24.182 --> 00:36:26.117
Nearly wet himself
when we reeled in this.

491
00:36:29.621 --> 00:36:32.318
Those bomblets were designed
in the '60s to carry sarin.

492
00:36:32.824 --> 00:36:34.664
What do you think the
range is on that missile?

493
00:36:35.193 --> 00:36:36.873
Depending on the
weight of those bomblets.

494
00:36:36.995 --> 00:36:40.329
I guess it could release high
enough to blanket a 20-mile radius.

495
00:36:40.498 --> 00:36:42.262
You wanted to see me?

496
00:36:42.634 --> 00:36:46.162
Back in Hong Kong. you
mentioned seeing some missiles.

497
00:36:46.838 --> 00:36:48.500
Yellow with red tips.

498
00:36:49.541 --> 00:36:52.978
These are the same ones
Peng was moving in Guangzhou.

499
00:36:54.379 --> 00:36:55.813
The day my brother was killed.

500
00:36:56.581 --> 00:36:57.981
Oh!

501
00:37:02.320 --> 00:37:03.379
Green mist.

502
00:37:05.824 --> 00:37:10.057
Kyoko in her fever. she was murmuring
about a green mist that came in the night.

503
00:38:35.580 --> 00:38:39.381
The active ingredient in the green
powder is a specially designed lectin.

504
00:38:39.751 --> 00:38:42.380
It's binding to the
glycoproteins of the red flu.

505
00:38:42.554 --> 00:38:45.752
That's why the virus looks
bulkier. It hasn't mutated.

506
00:38:46.324 --> 00:38:48.589
The lectin can create a
coating that shields the virus

507
00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:51.229
from the effects of the
antibody that our cure produces.

508
00:38:51.429 --> 00:38:53.607
I couldn't see it because I
didn't know what I was looking for.

509
00:38:53.631 --> 00:38:55.991
- But if somebody already has the cure?
- Then they're safe.

510
00:38:56.067 --> 00:38:57.745
You'd have to have the
lectin in your bloodstream first

511
00:38:57.769 --> 00:39:01.206
to render the cure ineffective.

512
00:39:02.106 --> 00:39:03.626
<i>That's what Peng's hoarding.</i>

513
00:39:04.209 --> 00:39:06.576
He could fire those missiles
over uncured populations.

514
00:39:07.612 --> 00:39:10.605
<i>- So when the cure finally does arrive...</i>
- It doesn't work.

515
00:39:10.915 --> 00:39:13.646
That boat was headed
to Taiwan on a run.

516
00:39:14.152 --> 00:39:15.711
Jesse saw the
missiles near Vietnam...

517
00:39:16.154 --> 00:39:18.214
And my wife saw
the mist in Japan.

518
00:39:19.557 --> 00:39:23.324
By the time we got to the
ports to receive the cure.

519
00:39:24.062 --> 00:39:25.621
it was already too late.

520
00:39:28.333 --> 00:39:29.460
That's right.

521
00:39:34.038 --> 00:39:36.530
I would like to see my wife.

522
00:39:37.275 --> 00:39:38.368
my son.

523
00:40:06.037 --> 00:40:08.734
- Good evening. Mr. President.
- Commander Green.

524
00:40:10.141 --> 00:40:11.200
<i>That's correct.</i>

525
00:40:13.211 --> 00:40:15.578
The President would
like to keep these briefings

526
00:40:15.747 --> 00:40:18.080
to senior advisors
for the time being.

527
00:40:19.484 --> 00:40:20.918
We'll summon you if we need you.

528
00:40:31.329 --> 00:40:33.491
<i>We were welcomed
as heroes in Vietnam.</i>

529
00:40:34.432 --> 00:40:36.492
Everyone came out of
hiding to get the cure.

530
00:40:39.370 --> 00:40:40.861
If they were exposed to this...

531
00:40:41.039 --> 00:40:44.009
They'd spread out across the
country to pass on the contagious cure.

532
00:40:44.475 --> 00:40:46.603
<i>And if they were
exposed to the red flu.</i>

533
00:40:48.279 --> 00:40:49.679
spread that instead.

534
00:40:49.847 --> 00:40:51.372
That was 10 days ago.

535
00:40:54.686 --> 00:40:57.155
And we don't know how many
of these missiles there are.

536
00:40:57.989 --> 00:41:01.323
So. now we know
what Peng's plan is.

537
00:41:05.029 --> 00:41:06.395
It's genocide.

538
00:41:47.672 --> 00:41:48.672
English -SDH

538
